505":{"id":"/docs/discord/commands-37","page_id":"/docs/discord/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/commands#help-and-about","content":"`/panel` and `/blacklist` are staff-gated. If someone without the right role runs them they get\n`You need the **Manage Server** permission to use this command.`"},"506":{"id":"/docs/discord","page_id":"/docs/discord","type":"page","content":"How a ticket opens","breadcrumbs":["dat one ticketer","In Discord"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord"},"507":{"id":"/docs/discord-0","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord","content":"The flow from a user clicking a panel to the welcome message appearing."},"508":{"id":"/docs/discord-1","page_id":"/docs/discord","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord#the-flow","content":"The flow"},"509":{"id":"/docs/discord-2","page_id":"/docs/discord","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord#permissions-inside-a-ticket","content":"Permissions inside a ticket"},"510":{"id":"/docs/discord-3","page_id":"/docs/discord","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord#naming","content":"Naming"},"511":{"id":"/docs/discord-4","page_id":"/docs/discord","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord#pings-on-open","content":"Pings on open"},"512":{"id":"/docs/discord-5","page_id":"/docs/discord","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord#limits-and-blacklist","content":"Limits and blacklist"},"513":{"id":"/docs/discord-6","page_id":"/docs/discord","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord#if-something-fails","content":"If something fails"},"514":{"id":"/docs/discord-7","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord","content":"This page describes what happens in Discord itself. It applies whether you use a channel panel\n(dropdown or buttons) or the slash commands."},"515":{"id":"/docs/discord-8","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#the-flow","content":"A user clicks a **dropdown** option or a **button** on a panel."},"516":{"id":"/docs/discord-9","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#the-flow","content":"If the chosen type has **sub-types**, a second menu appears - the user picks one."},"517":{"id":"/docs/discord-10","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#the-flow","content":"The bot checks the **blacklist** and the user's **open-ticket limits**."},"518":{"id":"/docs/discord-11","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#the-flow","content":"The bot creates a **private channel** or a **private thread**."},"519":{"id":"/docs/discord-12","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#the-flow","content":"The bot posts a **welcome message** with buttons, and pings the opener and your roles."},"520":{"id":"/docs/discord-13","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#the-flow","content":"The user gets an ephemeral confirmation linking to the new ticket."},"521":{"id":"/docs/discord-14","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#the-flow","content":"After that, the ticket is managed with the buttons inside it or the\n`/ticket` commands."},"522":{"id":"/docs/discord-15","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#permissions-inside-a-ticket","content":"**Channel tickets** are private. The bot sets permission overwrites so that:"},"523":{"id":"/docs/discord-16","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#permissions-inside-a-ticket","content":"`@everyone` cannot view the channel."},"524":{"id":"/docs/discord-17","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#permissions-inside-a-ticket","content":"The opener can view, send, read history, attach files and embed links."},"525":{"id":"/docs/discord-18","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#permissions-inside-a-ticket","content":"The bot itself can do the above plus manage messages."},"526":{"id":"/docs/discord-19","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#permissions-inside-a-ticket","content":"Your **staff roles** get the same as staff."},"527":{"id":"/docs/discord-20","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#permissions-inside-a-ticket","content":"Your **admin roles** additionally get **Manage Channels**."},"528":{"id":"/docs/discord-21","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#permissions-inside-a-ticket","content":"**Thread tickets** are private threads created under the panel's thread-parent channel (or the\npanel channel). The opener is added as a member; `invitable` is off. Threads auto-archive after\n7 days (10080 minutes) of inactivity."},"529":{"id":"/docs/discord-22","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#permissions-inside-a-ticket","content":"The bot adds the opener to the thread, but **not your staff roles**. A private thread is only\nvisible to its members and to users with **Manage Threads**, so give your staff that permission\nor have them use **Add User** on each ticket. If you would rather not hand out **Manage Threads**,\nuse `Private channel` mode - there your staff roles are granted access directly."},"530":{"id":"/docs/discord-23","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#naming","content":"The channel/thread name is built from the naming scheme (server default, overridden per type).\nSee the naming tokens table."},"531":{"id":"/docs/discord-24","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#pings-on-open","content":"The welcome message pings:"},"532":{"id":"/docs/discord-25","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#pings-on-open","content":"the **opener**, if **Ping the opener** is on; and"},"533":{"id":"/docs/discord-26","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#pings-on-open","content":"the **role IDs to ping** if you set any, otherwise your **staff roles**."},"534":{"id":"/docs/discord-27","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#pings-on-open","content":"This is what actually summons staff to a new ticket. If nobody pings, check\nCustomization → Mention pings."},"535":{"id":"/docs/discord-28","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#limits-and-blacklist","content":"**Blacklisted users** get an ephemeral \"You're not allowed to open tickets in this server\"\nmessage, with the reason if one was set."},"536":{"id":"/docs/discord-29","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#limits-and-blacklist","content":"Regular users are capped by **Max open tickets per user**, and optionally a per-type cap."},"537":{"id":"/docs/discord-30","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#limits-and-blacklist","content":"**Staff** bypass all open-ticket limits (they can always open a ticket to test)."},"538":{"id":"/docs/discord-31","page_id":"/docs/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord#if-something-fails","content":"If the bot can't create the channel (missing permissions, bad category, etc.) the user sees\n`Sorry, I couldn't create your ticket: <reason>`. Fix the permission or channel and try again -\nsee Troubleshooting."},"539":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","type":"page","content":"Panels in Discord","breadcrumbs":["dat one ticketer","In Discord"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/panels"},"540":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-0","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels","content":"Dropdowns, buttons, sub-types, and the panel message itself."},"541":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-1","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/panels#panel-types","content":"Panel types"},"542":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-2","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/panels#sub-types","content":"Sub-types"},"543":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-3","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/panels#the-panel-embed","content":"The panel embed"},"544":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-4","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/panels#re-posting-a-panel","content":"Re-posting a panel"},"545":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-5","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/panels#listing-and-deleting","content":"Listing and deleting"},"546":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-6","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels","content":"A panel is a message with a **dropdown** or **buttons**. It is posted by the dashboard (or\n`/panel create`) and edited in place whenever you save the panel. You can also re-post it with\n`/panel resend`."},"547":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-7","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels#panel-types","content":"| Style      | UI              | Max types |\n| ---------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| `Dropdown` | One select menu | 25        |","table":"table-0"},"548":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-8","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels#panel-types","content":"| Style     | UI                  | Max types |\n| --------- | ------------------- | --------- |\n| `Buttons` | One button per type | 5         |","table":"table-0"},"549":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-9","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels#panel-types","content":"Each type can have an **emoji**, a **label** and a **description** (descriptions only appear on\ndropdowns)."},"550":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-10","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels#sub-types","content":"If a type lists sub-types, choosing it opens a **second select menu**\n(`Choose a <type> category:`). Options are the sub-types, up to 25. The chosen sub-type becomes the\nticket's subject."},"551":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-11","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels#sub-types","content":"To add sub-types, open the type's **Advanced** section in the\npanel editor and use the `Sub-types` field, one per line:"},"552":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-12","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels#the-panel-embed","content":"The embed shows your title, description, colour, footer, image and thumbnail, plus an\n**Available options** field listing every type. If you set a **button label / placeholder**, that's\nthe dropdown placeholder (or the button text)."},"553":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-13","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels#re-posting-a-panel","content":"If a panel message is deleted, saving the panel edits fail and the bot posts a fresh one. You can\nforce a re-post from Discord:"},"554":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-14","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels#re-posting-a-panel","content":"`/panel resend` deletes the old message (if any) and posts a new one in the panel's channel."},"555":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-15","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels#listing-and-deleting","content":"`/panel list` shows every panel with its ID, channel and mode."},"556":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-16","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels#listing-and-deleting","content":"`/panel delete` removes a panel and its types (and its message)."},"557":{"id":"/docs/discord/panels-17","page_id":"/docs/discord/panels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/panels#listing-and-deleting","content":"See the command reference for the exact arguments."},"558":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","type":"page","content":"Ticket buttons","breadcrumbs":["dat one ticketer","In Discord"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/tickets"},"559":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-0","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets","content":"Claim, add, remove, rename, close, priority, tags and internal notes."},"560":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-1","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/tickets#claim","content":"Claim"},"561":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-2","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/tickets#add-user--remove-user","content":"Add User / Remove User"},"562":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-3","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/tickets#rename","content":"Rename"},"563":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-4","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/tickets#close","content":"Close"},"564":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-5","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/tickets#priority","content":"Priority"},"565":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-6","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/tickets#tags","content":"Tags"},"566":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-7","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/discord/tickets#note","content":"Note"},"567":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-8","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets","content":"The welcome message posted in every ticket has two rows of buttons:"},"568":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-9","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets","content":"| Button                                                    | Rows  | Who can use it                                             |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Claim` / `Add User` / `Remove User` / `Rename` / `Close` | row 1 | Staff (claim/rename/add/remove) or staff + opener (close). |","table":"table-0"},"569":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-10","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets","content":"| Button                       | Rows  | Who can use it |\n| ---------------------------- | ----- | -------------- |\n| `Priority` / `Tags` / `Note` | row 2 | Staff only.    |","table":"table-0"},"570":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-11","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets","content":"Button labels, emoji and styles are all configurable - see\nButtons & priorities."},"571":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-12","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#claim","content":"Marks you as handling the ticket. The welcome embed gets a `Claimed by <you>` field. The message\nconfirms with your **Claimed** system text. Staff only."},"572":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-13","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#add-user--remove-user","content":"Opens a modal where you enter a **user ID or mention**."},"573":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-14","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#add-user--remove-user","content":"On a channel ticket this edits the channel's permission overwrites."},"574":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-15","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#add-user--remove-user","content":"On a thread ticket this adds/removes a thread member."},"575":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-16","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#add-user--remove-user","content":"The action is recorded on the ticket's member list. Staff only."},"576":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-17","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#rename","content":"Opens a modal for a **new channel name**. The name is sanitised (lowercased, non-alphanumerics\nbecome `-`, capped at 90 characters). Staff only."},"577":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-18","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#close","content":"Closes the ticket. **Staff or the ticket opener** can close."},"578":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-19","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#close","content":"Closing does the following:"},"579":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-20","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#close","content":"Marks the ticket `closed` and records who closed it (and when)."},"580":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-21","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#close","content":"Generates the **transcript** and posts it (with the HTML file) to your transcript channel, or the\nlog channel, or nowhere."},"581":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-22","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#close","content":"DMs the opener a copy if **DM the opener a copy of the transcript** is on."},"582":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-23","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#close","content":"Archives + locks the thread, **or** deletes the channel if **Delete the channel on close** is on,\notherwise renames it `closed-<number>`."},"583":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-24","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#close","content":"Posts the **Ticket closed** system message with a transcript note."},"584":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-25","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#close","content":"See Customization → Closing for the wording."},"585":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-26","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#priority","content":"Opens a select menu of your priorities. The welcome\nembed's `Priority` field updates. Staff only."},"586":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-27","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#tags","content":"Opens a modal for comma-separated tags (up to 12, each up to 24 characters). The welcome embed\ngets a `Tags` field. Staff only."},"587":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-28","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#note","content":"Opens a modal for an **internal note** (up to 1500 characters). Notes are:"},"588":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-29","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#note","content":"stored on the ticket,"},"589":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-30","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#note","content":"posted as an embed to your **log channel** (or transcript channel), and"},"590":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-31","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#note","content":"**never** shown to the opener or included in the transcript."},"591":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-32","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#note","content":"Staff only."},"592":{"id":"/docs/discord/tickets-33","page_id":"/docs/discord/tickets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/discord/tickets#note","content":"Everything staff-only is enforced server-side: buttons and slash commands both check your staff\nand admin roles (or **Manage Channels**)."},"593":{"id":"/docs/faq","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"page","content":"FAQ","breadcrumbs":["dat one ticketer"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq"},"594":{"id":"/docs/faq-0","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq","content":"Short answers to the questions people ask most."},"595":{"id":"/docs/faq-1","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#do-i-need-to-keep-the-bot-online-or-host-anything","content":"Do I need to keep the bot online or host anything?"},"596":{"id":"/docs/faq-2","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#do-i-need-any-privileged-intents","content":"Do I need any privileged intents?"},"597":{"id":"/docs/faq-3","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#how-much-does-it-cost","content":"How much does it cost?"},"598":{"id":"/docs/faq-4","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#can-i-have-more-than-one-panel","content":"Can I have more than one panel?"},"599":{"id":"/docs/faq-5","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#channels-or-threads","content":"Channels or threads?"},"600":{"id":"/docs/faq-6","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#how-many-ticket-types-per-panel","content":"How many ticket types per panel?"},"601":{"id":"/docs/faq-7","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#can-users-see-each-others-tickets","content":"Can users see each other's tickets?"},"602":{"id":"/docs/faq-8","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#are-internal-notes-visible-to-the-user","content":"Are internal notes visible to the user?"},"603":{"id":"/docs/faq-9","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#where-are-transcripts-stored","content":"Where are transcripts stored?"},"604":{"id":"/docs/faq-10","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#can-i-block-someone-from-opening-tickets","content":"Can I block someone from opening tickets?"},"605":{"id":"/docs/faq-11","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#can-i-change-the-wording-and-colours","content":"Can I change the wording and colours?"},"606":{"id":"/docs/faq-12","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#can-i-change-the-bots-name-and-avatar-in-my-server","content":"Can I change the bot's name and avatar in my server?"},"607":{"id":"/docs/faq-13","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#are-there-ready-made-panel-templates","content":"Are there ready-made panel templates?"},"608":{"id":"/docs/faq-14","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#why-cant-my-staff-see-thread-tickets","content":"Why can't my staff see thread tickets?"},"609":{"id":"/docs/faq-15","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#is-there-a-list-of-all-limits","content":"Is there a list of all limits?"},"610":{"id":"/docs/faq-16","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#where-are-the-terms-and-privacy-policy","content":"Where are the Terms and Privacy Policy?"},"611":{"id":"/docs/faq-17","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#does-it-support-other-languages","content":"Does it support other languages?"},"612":{"id":"/docs/faq-18","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#is-it-open-source-can-i-self-host-it","content":"Is it open source? Can I self-host it?"},"613":{"id":"/docs/faq-19","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#do-i-need-to-keep-the-bot-online-or-host-anything","content":"No. dat one ticketer is a hosted service. There's nothing for you to run or keep alive - you just\ninvite the bot and it works."},"614":{"id":"/docs/faq-20","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#do-i-need-any-privileged-intents","content":"No. It only reacts to the buttons, commands and menus it posts; it never reads ordinary chat\nmessages."},"615":{"id":"/docs/faq-21","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#how-much-does-it-cost","content":"Nothing to you - just invite the bot and use it."},"616":{"id":"/docs/faq-22","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#can-i-have-more-than-one-panel","content":"Yes - as many as you like, in different channels, each with its own types, style, channels and\noverrides. Use **Duplicate** to copy one."},"617":{"id":"/docs/faq-23","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#channels-or-threads","content":"Both. Set it server-wide and override per panel (or per nothing - channels and threads are a\npanel-level choice). Threads are private, auto-archive after 7 days, and are archived + locked on\nclose instead of deleted."},"618":{"id":"/docs/faq-24","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#how-many-ticket-types-per-panel","content":"25 with **Dropdown**, 5 with **Buttons** (Discord's row limit)."},"619":{"id":"/docs/faq-25","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#can-users-see-each-others-tickets","content":"No. Tickets are private - only the opener, staff/admin roles and anyone explicitly added can see\nthem."},"620":{"id":"/docs/faq-26","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#are-internal-notes-visible-to-the-user","content":"No. Notes are stored on the ticket, posted to the log channel, and never shown to the opener or\nincluded in transcripts."},"621":{"id":"/docs/faq-27","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#where-are-transcripts-stored","content":"They're kept by the service (so they show up in the **Transcripts** tab) and posted to your\ntranscript or log channel as an HTML file. The opener can also get a DM copy."},"622":{"id":"/docs/faq-28","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#can-i-block-someone-from-opening-tickets","content":"Yes - use the **Ticket blacklist** (dashboard) or `/blacklist add`."},"623":{"id":"/docs/faq-29","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#can-i-change-the-wording-and-colours","content":"Yes, extensively - server-wide, per panel and (for some fields) per ticket type. See\nCustomization."},"624":{"id":"/docs/faq-30","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#can-i-change-the-bots-name-and-avatar-in-my-server","content":"Yes. The **Bot profile (this server)** card sets a nickname, avatar, banner and bio for your server\nonly. See Server profile."},"625":{"id":"/docs/faq-31","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#are-there-ready-made-panel-templates","content":"Yes - `Support`, `Sales`, `Report a user` and `Ban appeal`, plus `Blank`. See\nPanel templates."},"626":{"id":"/docs/faq-32","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#why-cant-my-staff-see-thread-tickets","content":"Private threads only show up for their members and users with **Manage Threads**. The bot adds the\nopener but not your staff roles. Grant **Manage Threads**, **Add User** the staff member, or use\nchannel tickets instead. See How a ticket opens."},"627":{"id":"/docs/faq-33","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#is-there-a-list-of-all-limits","content":"Yes - Limits & quotas covers panels, types, ticket fields and dashboard\nlists."},"628":{"id":"/docs/faq-34","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#where-are-the-terms-and-privacy-policy","content":"Both are linked in the dashboard header and footer: `/terms.html` and `/privacy.html`. They are\nsummarised on Terms & privacy."},"629":{"id":"/docs/faq-35","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#does-it-support-other-languages","content":"The UI text can be preset to English, Spanish, French, German or Portuguese, and every message is\neditable, so you can write it in any language."},"630":{"id":"/docs/faq-36","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#is-it-open-source-can-i-self-host-it","content":"No. dat one ticketer is closed source and only runs as the hosted service - you use it by inviting\nthe bot to your server."},"631":{"id":"/docs/getting-started","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"page","content":"Getting started","breadcrumbs":["dat one ticketer"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started"},"632":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started","content":"Invite the bot, sign in, and open your first ticket."},"633":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#1-invite-the-bot-to-your-server","content":"1. Invite the bot to your server"},"634":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-2","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#2-sign-in-to-the-dashboard","content":"2. Sign in to the dashboard"},"635":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-3","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"3. Do the one-minute config"},"636":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-4","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"4. Create your first panel"},"637":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-5","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#5-test-it","content":"5. Test it"},"638":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-6","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"Where to next"},"639":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started","content":"This is the fast path. Ten minutes end to end."},"640":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#1-invite-the-bot-to-your-server","content":"Open the dashboard at\n`dat-one-ticketer.danhost.workers.dev`."},"641":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#1-invite-the-bot-to-your-server","content":"Click **Invite the bot** (or **Add to Server**). This opens Discord's authorise screen."},"642":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#1-invite-the-bot-to-your-server","content":"Pick your server and approve. The bot needs the permissions it lists - see\nPermissions if you want to know why."},"643":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#2-sign-in-to-the-dashboard","content":"On the landing page click **Sign in with Discord**."},"644":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#2-sign-in-to-the-dashboard","content":"Authorise the app."},"645":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#2-sign-in-to-the-dashboard","content":"You land on **Servers** (`#/`). You see every server where you are the **owner** or have\n**Manage Server** - others are hidden."},"646":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#2-sign-in-to-the-dashboard","content":"To sign out later, use the sign-out link in the header."},"647":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"You can do all of this from the dashboard, or from Discord with slash commands."},"648":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"Open your server in the dashboard and, in **General settings**:"},"649":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"Set **Default ticket mode** - `Private channel` or `Private thread`."},"650":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"Set **Default category** - where new channel tickets go."},"651":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"Set **Staff roles** - who is allowed to claim and manage tickets."},"652":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"Set **Log channel** and **Transcript channel** (optional but recommended)."},"653":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"Click **Save settings**."},"654":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-22","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"If the server page shows **\"Add the bot to continue\"**, click **Add to Server** before anything\nelse - nothing works until the bot is actually in the server."},"655":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-23","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"On the server page, in the **Ticket panels** card, click **+ New panel**."},"656":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-24","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"Pick a template in **Start from a template** - `Support`, `Sales`, `Report a user` or\n`Ban appeal` - or leave it on `Blank`."},"657":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-25","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"Set **Channel to post in** and the **Title** / **Description** users will see."},"658":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-26","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"Add at least one **Ticket type** (a label like `General Support`)."},"659":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-27","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"Click **Create panel**."},"660":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-28","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"The panel message is posted to the channel you chose. Users can now click it to open a ticket."},"661":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-29","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#5-test-it","content":"Open Discord, go to the panel channel, and click the panel as if you were a user. You should get a\nprivate channel/thread with a welcome message and a row of buttons."},"662":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-30","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#5-test-it","content":"Then:"},"663":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-31","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#5-test-it","content":"Click **Claim** to take the ticket."},"664":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-32","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#5-test-it","content":"Click **Close** to close it - a transcript is generated and sent to your transcript (or log)\nchannel."},"665":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-33","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"<Card title=\"Launch checklist\" href=\"/docs/checklist\" />"},"666":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-34","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"<Card title=\"Setup recipes\" href=\"/docs/recipes\" />"},"667":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-35","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"<Card title=\"Tour the dashboard\" href=\"/docs/dashboard\" />"},"668":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-36","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"<Card title=\"Full settings reference\" href=\"/docs/dashboard/settings\" />"},"669":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-37","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"<Card title=\"Slash commands\" href=\"/docs/discord/commands\" />"},"670":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-38","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"<Card title=\"Placeholders\" href=\"/docs/customization/placeholders\" />"},"671":{"id":"/docs/glossary","page_id":"/docs/glossary","type":"page","content":"Glossary","breadcrumbs":["dat one ticketer"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/glossary"},"672":{"id":"/docs/glossary-0","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"The words dat one ticketer uses, and what they mean."},"673":{"id":"/docs/glossary-1","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Admin role**\n: A higher-tier staff role. Admins additionally get **Manage Channels** inside channel tickets."},"674":{"id":"/docs/glossary-2","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Audit log**\n: A reverse-chronological record of settings, panel, blacklist and ticket changes, each with an\nactor ID and timestamp."},"675":{"id":"/docs/glossary-3","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Blacklist**\n: A list of users who cannot open tickets in a server."},"676":{"id":"/docs/glossary-4","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Bot profile**\n: The nickname, avatar, banner and bio the bot shows in one server, set on the server page. It does\nnot change the bot globally."},"677":{"id":"/docs/glossary-5","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Button panel**\n: A panel that shows one button per ticket type (max 5)."},"678":{"id":"/docs/glossary-6","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Channel ticket**\n: A private channel created for a single ticket."},"679":{"id":"/docs/glossary-7","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Claim**\n: A staff member marking themselves as handling a ticket."},"680":{"id":"/docs/glossary-8","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Customization**\n: The messages, colours, buttons and priorities that shape how tickets look and read. Set\nserver-wide, per panel, and per type."},"681":{"id":"/docs/glossary-9","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Dropdown panel**\n: A panel that shows a select menu of ticket types (max 25)."},"682":{"id":"/docs/glossary-10","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Internal note**\n: A staff-only note on a ticket. Never shown to the opener and never included in transcripts."},"683":{"id":"/docs/glossary-11","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Log channel**\n: The channel that receives ticket activity and internal notes. Also used for transcripts when no\ntranscript channel is set."},"684":{"id":"/docs/glossary-12","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Max open tickets**\n: The per-user cap on open tickets. Staff bypass it, and a ticket type can add its own cap."},"685":{"id":"/docs/glossary-13","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Panel**\n: A message in a channel with a dropdown or buttons that opens tickets."},"686":{"id":"/docs/glossary-14","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Panel template**\n: A starting point in the new-panel editor - `Blank`, `Support`, `Sales`, `Report a user` or\n`Ban appeal`. It fills in the panel message and ticket types; everything stays editable."},"687":{"id":"/docs/glossary-15","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Placeholder**\n: A `{token}` in a text field that is replaced with a real value, e.g. `{username}`."},"688":{"id":"/docs/glossary-16","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Priority**\n: Low / Normal / High / Urgent (or your own list). Used by the Priority button and shown on the\nwelcome embed."},"689":{"id":"/docs/glossary-17","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Private thread**\n: A thread only visible to its members and users with **Manage Threads**. Used for thread tickets."},"690":{"id":"/docs/glossary-18","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Staff**\n: Anyone with **Manage Channels**, or any role listed in Staff roles or Admin roles."},"691":{"id":"/docs/glossary-19","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Sub-type**\n: A second choice under a ticket type, e.g. `Bug report → Crash`."},"692":{"id":"/docs/glossary-20","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Tag**\n: A short free-text label staff can put on a ticket."},"693":{"id":"/docs/glossary-21","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Ticket**\n: A single support conversation, opened from a panel and living in its own channel or thread."},"694":{"id":"/docs/glossary-22","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Ticket type**\n: One option on a panel, e.g. `General Support` or `Sales`."},"695":{"id":"/docs/glossary-23","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Transcript**\n: A styled HTML copy of a ticket's messages, generated when the ticket closes."},"696":{"id":"/docs/glossary-24","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Transcript channel**\n: The channel where closed-ticket transcripts are posted. Falls back to the log channel, and the\ntranscript is always saved even if neither is set."},"697":{"id":"/docs/glossary-25","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Thread ticket**\n: A private thread created for a single ticket (auto-archives after 7 days; archived + locked on\nclose)."},"698":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["dat one ticketer"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"699":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"What dat one ticketer is, where you use it, and what it can do."},"700":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#the-two-places-you-use-it","content":"The two places you use it"},"701":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"What it can do"},"702":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#who-this-wiki-is-for","content":"Who this wiki is for"},"703":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"**dat one ticketer** is a Discord ticketing bot. Users click a panel in your server, a private\nchannel or thread opens for them, and your staff manage it with buttons or slash commands. Every\nticket can be exported as an HTML transcript when it closes."},"704":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"It's a hosted service - you just invite the bot. There's nothing to install and nothing to keep\nonline, and a dashboard where you set everything up and read your ticket history."},"705":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-two-places-you-use-it","content":"| Place                 | What for                                                                                                                             |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **The web dashboard** | Set everything up: panels, ticket types, messages, colours, channels, staff roles, blacklists, transcripts, stats and the audit log. |","table":"table-0"},"706":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-two-places-you-use-it","content":"| Place       | What for                                                                                       |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Discord** | Where users open tickets from a panel and staff claim, rename, tag, prioritise and close them. |","table":"table-0"},"707":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-two-places-you-use-it","content":"You sign in to the dashboard **with Discord**. In Discord itself you only need the bot in your\nserver - use the **Add to Server** / **Invite the bot** button."},"708":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-two-places-you-use-it","content":"The dashboard lives at\n`dat-one-ticketer.danhost.workers.dev`."},"709":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"A message with a dropdown or buttons. Each option is a ticket type (\"Bug report\",\n\"Ban appeal\", ...). Post as many panels as you like."},"710":{"id":"/docs-11","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"Each ticket opens either as a private channel or a private thread, server-wide or per panel or\nper type."},"711":{"id":"/docs-12","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"When a ticket closes, a styled HTML copy of every message is saved, posted to a channel, and\noptionally DMed to the opener."},"712":{"id":"/docs-13","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"Welcome embeds, button labels/emoji/styles, custom priorities, all system messages and the\ntranscript embed - with `{placeholders}`."},"713":{"id":"/docs-14","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"Claim, add/remove users, rename, tags, internal notes (never shown to the user) and priorities."},"714":{"id":"/docs-15","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"A nickname, avatar, banner and bio for the bot in your server alone."},"715":{"id":"/docs-16","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"Complete configurations for support, reports, sales and ban appeals."},"716":{"id":"/docs-17","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"The short list to run through before you announce your panel."},"717":{"id":"/docs-18","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"Totals, open counts, per-staff claimed/closed counts, and a reverse-chronological log of every\nchange."},"718":{"id":"/docs-19","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/d